WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.940
When software can move a machine,

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.520
its decisions enter a
world shared with people.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.780
Bounder explores how a
clear boundary can accompany

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:14.040
that movement, so that every
requested action remains within

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.700
an explicitly defined scope.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.860
The process begins with human
and organisational intent.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.040
Creed Space Fleet translates that
intent into protective policy

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.180
for a particular device,

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.920
specifying the conditions
under which it may act.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.900
That policy travels in a signed envelope.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.280
The local Guardian
checks its authenticity,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.220
its intended recipient and its validity,

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.120
connecting the permission
that was issued to the device

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.140
that receives it.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.400
Before an action proceeds,

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.780
Bounder evaluates the request
against verified policy,

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.400
current platform state and fresh evidence.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:52.120
A device-specific adapter then
translates the bounded result

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:54.820
into the safest response
available for that platform.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.480
This separation matters
when connectivity fails.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.040
An unavailable audit channel
cannot change the local decision,

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.600
while cached authority still expires.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.780
Communication problems remain
distinct from the question

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.300
of whether movement is permitted.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.440
Each decision leaves a signed receipt,

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.100
linking the outcome to the
inputs and authority behind

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:16.300
it.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.420
These records support accountability,

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.560
allowing a reviewer to follow
what happened without turning

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.140
evidence into a new permission.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.440
Bounder is currently simulation-only.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.240
Its public browser laboratory lets
you explore recorded scenarios,

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.180
inspect published contracts and
verify supplied evidence locally,

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.040
while physical safety remains
a separate engineering

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.840
and validation responsibility.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.460
For engineers and researchers,

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.580
it offers a concrete
architecture to examine:

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.400
explicit authority, local evaluation,

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.340
bounded response and inspectable evidence,

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:52.060
carried together from
an intention to the edge

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.100
of physical action.
